    "updated_at": "2022-04-04T20:19:17Z",
    "body": "Thanks for clarifying.\r\n\r\n> > Why not to use modern bash on Mac?\r\n> \r\n> Most users will have the default shell installed because there's no really pressing reason to upgrade, and this makes Starship look bad.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, upgrading bash isn't necessarily easy or safe, otherwise I'd do it. Bash is a relatively low-level soft dependency managed by the distro itself.\r\n\r\nI looked into how I could update bash for Ubuntu 20.04 (LTS), and I'm nervous about pulling the trigger. I'd have to add an Ubuntu 21+ repo, then update `/etc/apt/preferences.d/` to make sure *only* bash gets updated to 5.1. Who knows what that would do to my bash auto-complete scripts and whatnot, which think they're running on Ubuntu 20.04's version of bash.",
