    "updated_at": "2022-04-07T15:32:58Z",
    "body": "Unfortunately, I'm still seeing the issue with the fix for https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/3793. I built master from source (230e85be37a0fc12999d1e6ff1209e7d5f99ecd1) and the line wrap on long commands (anything more than one line) still looks like this:\r\n\r\n`to fit on one line\"Here is my commit message that is too long`\r\n\r\nAnother oddity, one that's hard to describe: when there's a command in my history that exceeds 1 line, every time I \"visit\" that command, one line of my terminal output is cleared. \r\n\r\n1. run \"long\" command: `echo 'this is a line that's too long to fit in my terminal without wrapping'`\r\n2. hit the up arrow to show the \"long\" command from history\r\n3. hit the up arrow again to some \"short\" command\r\n4. note the terminal output shrunk by one line\r\n5. hit the down arrow to return to the \"long\" command\r\n6. hit the down arrow to \"exit\" history and return to prompt\r\n7. note that another line from the terminal disappeared\r\n\r\nI assume the two issues are related.\r\n\r\nFWIW, the behavior is the same for `add_newline = true` and `add_newline = false`",
